 part 1 of Darwin: distinct species, under domestication, under nature, domestic races, many generations, state of nature, animals and plants


@sen45    I am fully convinced that species are not immutable; but that those belonging to what are called the same genera are lineal descendants of some other and generally extinct species, in the same manner as the acknowledged varieties of any one species are the descendants of that species.

              " (extract-fr) part 1 of Darwin: distinct species, under domestication, under nature, domestic races, many generations, state of nature, animals and plants

@sen46    Furthermore, I am convinced that natural selection has been the most important, but not the exclusive, means of modification.

              " (extract-fr) part 1 of Darwin: distinct species, under domestication, under nature, domestic races, many generations, state of nature, animals and plants

